{
 "cells": [
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Type II OPE Unit Tests\n\nUnit tests for OPE computations of fundamental Type IIB worldsheet operators using Ashoke conventions:\n- Matter free fermion (psi, psit)\n- xi-eta ghost system\n- Linear dilaton (dphi, dphit)\n- Exponentials of phi (expPhib, expPhif)",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "Needs[\"StringCode`\"]\nStringCode`InitStringCode[<|\"theory\" -> \"TypeII\", \"CFT\" -> \"FlatSpace\", \"conventions\"-> \"TypeII-Ashoke\", \"bracket\"->\"Flat\"|>]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {
    "timing": {
     "startTime": 1770485136127,
     "endTime": 1770485136251
    },
    "executionOrder": 3,
    "success": true
   }
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Matter Free Fermion Tests (psi, psit)\n\nThe matter free fermion has the OPE (in Ashoke conventions with fermionToBosonWickRatio = -1/2):\n$$\\psi^\\mu(z) \\psi^\\nu(w) \\sim -\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{\\delta^{\\mu\\nu}}{z-w}$$",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Test 1: Basic psi-psi contraction\n\nWick[psi[mu,0,z], psi[nu,0,w]] should give -1/2 * delta[mu,nu]/(z-w)",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "test1 = Wick[\\[Psi][\\[Mu], 0, z], \\[Psi][\\[Nu], 0, w]];\nexpected1 = -1/2 \\[Delta][\\[Mu], \\[Nu]]/(z - w);\ntest1Result = Simplify[test1 - expected1] === 0;\nPrint[\"Test 1 (psi-psi Wick): \", If[test1Result, \"PASSED\", \"FAILED\"]];\ntest1Result",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<pre>Test 1 (psi-psi Wick): PASSED\n</pre>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "\"Test 1 (psi-psi Wick): PASSED\\n\"",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "7ee1a2fa-8e27-44cd-a766-47dd716cafad",
     "metadata": {
      "cellLabel": "",
      "isBoxData": false
     }
    },
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wexpr\"><w>True</w></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "True",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "79882c2c-56ac-4482-8146-503681340206",
     "metadata": {
      "cellLabel": "Out[9]= ",
      "isBoxData": false
     }
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {
    "timing": {
     "startTime": 1770485136252,
     "endTime": 1770485136653
    },
    "executionOrder": 5,
    "success": true
   }
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Test 2: Derivative psi with psi\n\nWick[psi[mu,1,z], psi[nu,0,w]] = d_z(-1/2 * delta/(z-w)) = 1/2 * delta/(z-w)^2",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "test2 = Wick[\\[Psi][\\[Mu], 1, z], \\[Psi][\\[Nu], 0, w]];\nexpected2 = 1/2 \\[Delta][\\[Mu], \\[Nu]]/(z - w)^2;\ntest2Result = Simplify[test2 - expected2] === 0;\nPrint[\"Test 2 (dpsi-psi Wick): \", If[test2Result, \"PASSED\", \"FAILED\"]];\ntest2Result",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
